      "text": "Retirement delays of U.S. electric generating capacity may continue in 2026 - U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA)"
    },
    {
      "start": 196,
      "end": 779,
      "text": "Retirement delays of U.S. electric generating capacity may continue in 2026\nData source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, Preliminary Monthly Electric Generator Inventory , December 2025\nU.S. power plant owners and operators plan to retire nearly 11 gigawatts (GW) of utility-scale electric generating capacity from the U.S. power grid this year, according to data reported to us in our latest Preliminary Monthly Electric Generator Inventory . Almost all the scheduled retirements are either coal-fired power plants (58%) or steam turbines and simple-cycle natural gas (42%)."
    }
